Because Scraping APIs charge a fixed &lt;strong&gt;25 credits per request&lt;/strong&gt; regardless of page weight, a 1.5 MB page costs the exact same as a 100 KB page. On Apify, 1.5 MB/page across 100k pages equals &lt;strong&gt;150 GB&lt;/strong&gt;, which alone costs &lt;strong&gt;$1,050/mo&lt;/strong&gt; even on Business ($7.00/GB).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;(What if you block images, fonts, and third-party scripts in Playwright down to **0.25 MB/page&lt;/em&gt;* = 25 GB total? On Apify Scale, 200 CUs × $0.16 + 25 GB × $7.50 = $32 + $187.50 = &lt;strong&gt;$219.50/mo&lt;/strong&gt;—competitive with ScrapingBee Business at $249 and ScraperAPI Business at $299, though still slightly above Scrapingdog Pro at $200.)*&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


4. Benchmark 2: 1,000,000 Pages / Month
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At &lt;strong&gt;1M pages/month&lt;/strong&gt;, the same split holds—and &lt;strong&gt;JavaScript-only (datacenter proxy)&lt;/strong&gt; workloads reveal a sweet spot for Apify Scale.&lt;/p&gt;

